{
    "background_story": "Jordyn was a talented forager who lived in a small village on the edge of a vast forest. She was particularly skilled at identifying and harvesting the elusive bitternut, a rare and prized type of walnut. Jordyn's knowledge of the forest and its secrets was unmatched, and she spent most of her days exploring the woods, searching for the perfect bitternut trees. Her passion for foraging was not just about gathering food, but about preserving the traditional ways of her community. Jordyn's bitternut harvests were always met with excitement, as the villagers would use them to make delicious oils, teas, and baked goods. Her dedication to her craft earned her the nickname 'Bitternut Jordyn,' and her reputation as a master forager spread far and wide.",
